    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py` to the spec, and wrote 37 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py` that import from `solution`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 37. The code uses `Decimal` throughout and rounds each line's net and tax to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, then sums those. The standard-category bulk discount (qty ≥ 10) multiplies on top of the line discount. Credit is applied against gross and is quantized to cents. Validation raises `ValueError` for an unknown region or category, a bad `qty` (including `bool`), a negative price or credit, and a discount outside 0–100. The tests cover those branches, the rounding edge cases, the bulk-discount boundary, and the output format. I haven't measured line coverage, since the coverage gate was not run here; the tests exercise every branch in `solution.py`, so it should clear 90%. One test expectation was wrong on the first run (a 3.00 credit against 10.00 gross leaves 0.00 credit), and I corrected the test, not the code.",
